abstract: >-
  The fraction of agent tool use that a serving stack silently discards grows
  with model scale, and it reaches the policy gradient. Four model families
  configured for function calling on vLLM each fail at a different layer;
  for Qwen2.5-Coder the server parses 0/100 calls at every scale from 1.5B to
  32B while well-formed emitted calls rise to 80/100. In RL training the same
  mismatch yields zero tool executions, rendering the tool-using policy branch
  unreachable by gradient.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - tool calling
  - evaluation validity
  - reinforcement learning
  - vLLM
